# Every non-comment, non-blank line is text the failure diagnostic must contain.
# The first pins the diagnostic's code (so an unrelated failure cannot satisfy it),
# the second the refusal, and the third the mode the call could not be reached in
# together with the mode it declares — which is what makes this a test of the
# feasibility pass rather than of "something went wrong".
